      "side": 1,
      "message": "TL;DR IIUC, we\u0027re good for T (since CompOS is only packaged in APEX and won\u0027t be a Mainline module in T), but must address this problem in U for turning into Mainline.\n\nThere are a few things to considers, looking into the future:\n\n1. CompOS won\u0027t be Mainline\u0027d in T (maybe in U).  So `__builtin_available(android __ANDROID_API_T__,*)` should be sufficient for now.\n\n2. CompOS APEX is optional, so only some T devices will have it.  There will be other guarding condition to trigger the ART code path.  The condition is still TBD: it could be a `ro.` system property as a feature flag, or if possible, detect automatically if we can detect sufficient pKVM/SoC support AND CompOS APEX exists.\n\n3. We plan to transition CompOS from (optional) platform feature to (optional) Mainline module.  It\u0027ll take a few years for SoCs to catch up before we can require it.\n\nConceptually, I\u0027m thinking the following pseudo code to cover the above.\n\n  ASSERT(CompOSIsAvailable()); // This ART code path shouldn\u0027t be trigger otherwise\n\n  // [Case 3 above] Say, CompOS is required by Z...\n  // On Z+ devices, ART can use CompOS API __INTRODUCED_IN(Z)\n  if (__builtin_available(android __ANDROID_API_Z__,*)) {\n    something_that_uses_compos_api_1();\n    return;\n  }\n\n  // [Case 2] CompOS will become an (optional) Mainline module from certain\n  // platform release.\n\n  // IF, CompOS introduces any new API with a Mainline update, ART may\n  // call the new API. This probably needs b/178774199.\n  if (__builtin_available(android __ANDROID_API_U_EXT_,*)) {\n    something_that_uses_compos_api_2();\n    return;\n  }\n  // Otherwise, ART can simply use CompOS API __INTRODUCED_IN(U).\n  if (__builtin_available(android __ANDROID_API_U__,*)) {\n    something_that_uses_compos_api_3();\n    return;\n  }\n\n  // [Case 1] For T release, where CompOS is not a Mainline module.\n  // On T devices, ART can use CompOS API __INTRODUCED_IN(T)\n  if (__builtin_available(android __ANDROID_API_T__,*)) {\n    something_that_uses_compos_api_4();\n    return;\n  }\n\nDoes it make sense? Hope I\u0027m not over thinking it.\n\nJiyong, WDYT? Also +hansson for input.",
      "parentUuid": "246e037e_b9181df6",
      "revId": "5b817e642c7643929d0219fed32a5d1e7acdbf14",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
